+### Compound Format
+
+Use `compound` to get multiple short units, largest first. It goes up to days and down to seconds; leftover milliseconds are dropped. It takes precedence over `long`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })             // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })            // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(40 * 86400000, { compound: true })       // "40d" (does not roll past days)
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })            // "-1h 30m"
+ms(999, { compound: true })                 // "0s"
+```
+
